      "message": "I\u0027m not opposed to the idea of carrying a size around so that `BindBufferInfo` can represent a slice of a buffer but I think it\u0027s awkward that it\u0027s only used for uniforms at the moment and everything is 0.\n\nThe down side to this is that a lot of other usage of BindBufferInfo while writing vertex/draw data should probably be updated as well, and their size would start out as the remainder of the buffer and then `DrawWriter` would reduce it based on what was actually utilized. This becomes a larger scale effort that is probably worth it, but I\u0027m wondering if we can get away with leaving BindBufferInfo as is for now and use one of the strategies I outlined in my other comment to get past the validation error?",
